-- title:
--   Finite flat complete intersections over a DVR are Gorenstein
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring that is a domain and a discrete valuation ring, and let $T$ be a commutative ring equipped with an $\mathcal O$-algebra structure such that $T$ is finite and free as an $\mathcal O$-module. Assume further that $T$ admits a complete intersection presentation with as many relations as variables: there exist a natural number $n$ and an $n$-tuple $f : \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to \mathcal O[[X_1,\dots,X_n]]$ of multivariate power series in $n$ variables over $\mathcal O$ together with an isomorphism of $\mathcal O$-algebras $\mathcal O[[X_1,\dots,X_n]]/(f_1,\dots,f_n) \xrightarrow{\sim} T$, the ideal being the one generated by the range of $f$ (the hypothesis asserts nonemptiness of the type of such isomorphisms). The conclusion is the existence of an $\mathcal O$-bilinear map $C : T \to T \to \mathcal O$, given as an $\mathcal O$-linear map into the $\mathcal O$-linear maps $T \to \mathcal O$, which is $T$-invariant in the sense that $C(st, u) = C(t, su)$ for all $s,t,u \in T$, and which is perfect in the sense that the map $t \mapsto C(t,-)$ is a bijection from $T$ onto $\mathrm{Hom}_{\mathcal O}(T,\mathcal O)$.
--
--   This is the Gorenstein property, relative to $\mathcal O$, of a finite flat complete intersection $T = \mathcal O[[X_1,\dots,X_n]]/(f_1,\dots,f_n)$: the $\mathcal O$-dual of $T$ is free of rank one over $T$, realised by an invariant perfect pairing. It supplies the self-duality of the rings produced by the patching and numerical-criterion arguments, and is used here in the proof of [`AlgHom.bijective_and_free_of_length_le`](thm.html#AlgHom.bijective_and_free_of_length_le).
